task-mesh (0.3.2~alpha1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Alpha pre-release for volunteer testing (T.A.S.K. Milestone B);
    approved 2026-11-23 for packaging, building and isolated testing only.
    UNVERIFIED on Raspberry Pi hardware.
  * Ship the audible Mesh alert that was hand-modified on the development
    Pi as maintained source (hub/notifier.py, SHA-256 2864d242...bbe1a): the
    desktop notification suppresses its own sound and the notifier plays
    ~/.local/share/task-mesh/sounds/mesh-alert.wav with /usr/bin/paplay
    (argv list, detached, no shell) when sound is on. The WAV itself is not
    shipped (CC-BY-SA-3.0 source); scripts/generate-mesh-alert.sh creates it.
  * No other code change from 0.3.1. Retention behaviour unchanged.
  * Tests: AT-15 crash-safety test uses a frozen reference clock (it failed
    after 2026-10-21 because fixed 2026-09-21 timestamps were pruned by the
    30-day startup retention).
  * Recommends pulseaudio-utils (paplay, used by the audible alert);
    Suggests ffmpeg and sound-theme-freedesktop (alert generator script).

 -- T.A.S.K. Development Team <TBD-maintainer-email>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:30:00 -0500

task-mesh (0.3.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 4F.1 corrective release.
  * Fix: with task-mesh-service running, the window opened the serial port
    itself on Connect/Retry and backed off with "Serial port is in use".
    The window now attaches to the service (service-client mode) whenever
    the service runs, also when the service starts after the window: it
    releases its own ports, never opens one, shows the service's states,
    receives live over the private socket and sends through the service
    (explicit Send + Core sign-in). The service is the only writer. When
    the service stops (after a 15 s grace for restarts) the window returns
    to direct mode without reconnecting automatically.
  * IPC: per-connection ids (client cannot spoof), live event stream with
    reconnect, focus leases (15 s TTL, dropped on disconnect), stop closes
    client connections. Still 0600 + same-uid peer credentials.
  * Notifications: title "T.A.S.K. — New Mesh Message", protocol/sender/
    preview only when allowed, generic when signed out, expire 5000 ms,
    burst grouping, no pop-up while a Mesh window is focused (nothing is
    marked read), click opens the conversation by internal id
    (--open-message ID). Session bus found via DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS or
    $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bus.
  * New task-mesh-notify-setup: read-only diagnosis; opt-in --enable writes a
    user D-Bus activation file for notification-daemon (Debian's package has
    none) and an LXDE login entry importing DISPLAY/XAUTHORITY.

 -- T.A.S.K. Development Team <TBD-maintainer-email>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:30:00 -0400

task-mesh (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 4F: one app for Meshtastic and MeshCore. Tabs: All Messages,
    Meshtastic, MeshCore, Devices, Network Status. Identities are never
    merged across protocols.
  * MeshCore companion (USB serial) via meshcore 2.3.15 (MIT, bundled with
    pycayennelpp 2.4.0 and pyserial-asyncio-fast 0.16). Read-only session
    commands; sending only from an explicit Send click.
  * Optional background receiver task-mesh-service (systemd --user unit,
    installed DISABLED, single instance, private 0600 socket). Without it
    the window owns the radios as before.
  * Per-device locks on /dev/serial/by-id; only user-assigned ports are
    opened; read-only identify on click; never flashes or changes settings.
  * Hub history (SQLite 0600), unread = live inbound only, explicit
    mark-read, retention setting; freedesktop notifications with preview,
    sound, per-protocol and per-conversation mute, quiet mode; generic
    "New Mesh Message" while signed out or locked.
  * Sending requires a Core session (operator or administrator).
  * New Depends: python3-pycryptodome, python3-jeepney,
    python3-task-comms (>= 0.3.1).

 -- T.A.S.K. Development Team <TBD-maintainer-email>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:30:00 -0400

task-mesh (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 4C: renamed from rain-mesh (Provides/Replaces/Breaks rain-mesh
    << 0.2.0~; transitional rain-mesh 0.2.0); channel messages and DMs
    with honest delivery states; private history behind a Core sign-in;
    status card; opt-in Maps geofeed; legacy rain-mesh data copied (never
    moved) on first start.

